# The owner is a required reviewer only for two things:
#   (a) guardrails: anything that, if silently weakened, would stop an agent
#       guardrail or a required check protecting us. That is the workflows and
#       actions that enforce checks or gate deploys, this file, ruleset and
#       branch-protection files, the gate tools and their tests, the floors
#       and ignore files that set gate levels, and the trust anchors that
#       decide who may sign a release.
#   (b) human-facing docs: the README and the licence text.
# Everything else is released: it merges on the reviewer App's approval and
# green CI. There is deliberately no catch-all line.
#
# GitHub applies the LAST matching line, so a line with no owner releases a
# path an earlier line owned. The released files sit after the owned groups and
# before the seven shared lines. Those seven come from the standards template and
# stay last, byte for byte, so the standards sync check passes.
#
# Matching is case-sensitive and has no character classes, so each name form
# below is spelled in lower-case, Capitalised and UPPER-case.

# Workflows and actions that enforce a check or gate a deploy. docs-lint-self.yml
# emits the one required check here ("docs-lint"); the reusable workflows are
# what the other repos' required checks and gated applies call (docs lint, opv
# lint, image scan, the gated apply and the gated step); every action is gate code.
# standards.yml and docs-lint.yml come from the shared lines at the end. The
# self-test workflows, the drift check, the nightly rescan, the scan report and
# Dependabot settings are released: nothing requires them and none gates a deploy.
/.github/workflows/docs-lint-self.yml          @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/workflows/opv-lint.yml                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/workflows/image-scan.yml              @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/workflows/ansible-gated-apply.yml     @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/workflows/ansible-gated-step.yml      @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
**/.github/actions/                            @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# CODEOWNERS and ruleset or branch-protection files: they say who must approve.
**/CODEOWNERS                                  @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
**/codeowners                                  @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
**/CodeOwners                                  @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
**/*ruleset*                                   @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
**/*Ruleset*                                   @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
**/*RULESET*                                   @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
**/*branch-protection*                         @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
**/*Branch-Protection*                         @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
**/*BRANCH-PROTECTION*                         @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
**/*branch_protection*                         @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
**/*Branch_Protection*                         @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
**/*BRANCH_PROTECTION*                         @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
**/*branchprotection*                          @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
**/*BranchProtection*                          @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
**/*BRANCHPROTECTION*                          @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# The gate code and its tests: the lint tools every repo's CI
# calls, the apply-gate tests, the hook registry that runs them, and the
# ignore files that switch checks off.
/tools/                                        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.pre-commit-hooks.yaml                        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.opv-lint*                                    @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/tools/floors.tsv                              @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# Trust anchors: the signer list that decides which release tags are trusted,
# and the trust directory the host-key checks read.
**/allowed_signers                             @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/ansible/trust/                                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# Human-facing docs and the owner's own words: the README and the licence text.
/README.md                                     @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/LICENSE                                       @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# Released: prose that explains a kept gate and that no job reads as input.
# These lines name no owner and must stay after every owned line above.
/tools/docs-lint-rules.md
/tools/opv-lint-rules.md
/tools/resolve-pinned-ref.md

# The shared set from the standards template. Keep these lines last.
/.standardsignore        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.standards.mode         @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.docs-lint*             @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.standards-db-tooling   @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/CODEOWNERS      @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/workflows/standards.yml  @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/workflows/docs-lint.yml  @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
